"Project: demo (ticket prefix DEMO)
Analysing the change…
Readiness: READY · risk low
  risk analyst: The cart endpoint might return an incorrect total (sum of unit price × quantity) if rounding or initial calculation is flawed.
  risk analyst: Applying discount codes might result in incorrect total reduction when a single valid code is applied (percentage reduction).
  risk analyst: The system may fail to correctly handle sequential discount codes, potentially allowing codes to stack instead of replacing the first one (AC3).
  risk analyst: The system may fail to return an appropriate 404 error with the code DISCOUNT_NOT_FOUND when an unknown discount code is submitted, leaving the total unchanged (AC4).
Writing the test plan…
Plan v1: 4 case(s), 0 open question(s)
<run>/plan/plan.v1.md
"
`;

exports[`replay of recorded model answers (REQ-LLM-14/AC5) > REQ-LLM-14/AC5: gemma4:e2b's analysis and plan for DEMO-1, invalid answers and repairs included, go through the current checks 2`] = `
"schema: 1
ticket: DEMO-1
version: 1
summary: Test cases verifying cart total calculation, discount application rules, and error handling for discount codes.
cases:
  - id: TC-01
    title: GET /cart returns total rounded once to 2 decimals (AC1)
    type: api
    priority: high
    reproduces: false
    source:
      - kind: ac
        id: AC1
    preconditions:
      - Cart contains multiple line items with prices and quantities.
    data:
      user: user:standard
    steps:
      - id: S1
        action: GET /cart
        expect:
          description: The total returned is the sum of (unit price × quantity) for all lines, rounded once to 2 decimals.
          status: 200
          fields:
            total: The calculated sum rounded to two decimal places
    evidence:
      - response
  - id: TC-02
    title: POST /cart/discount applies a single valid percentage discount (AC2)
    type: api
    priority: high
    reproduces: false
    source:
      - kind: ac
        id: AC2
    preconditions:
      - Cart total is calculated (e.g., $100.00). A valid discount code exists with a percentage.
    data:
      user: user:standard
    steps:
      - id: S1
        action: POST /cart/discount
        expect:
          description: Total is reduced by the code's percentage.
          status: 200
          fields:
            total: The cart total reflects the discount applied as a percentage reduction.
    evidence:
      - response
  - id: TC-03
    title: Applying a second valid code replaces the first (AC3)
    type: api
    priority: high
    reproduces: false
    source:
      - kind: ac
        id: AC3
    preconditions:
      - Cart contains items. A valid discount code (Code A) exists, and a second valid discount code (Code B) exists.
    data:
      user: user:standard
    steps:
      - id: S1
        action: POST /cart/discount
        expect:
          description: Apply the first valid discount code (Code A).
          status: 200
      - id: S2
        action: POST /cart/discount
        expect:
          description: Apply a second valid discount code (Code B), which must replace Code A. Codes must never stack.
          status: 200
          fields:
            total: The final total reflects the reduction based on Code B applied to the original total, ignoring Code A.
    evidence:
      - response
  - id: TC-04
    title: Applying an unknown discount code returns 404 with DISCOUNT_NOT_FOUND (AC4)
    type: api
    priority: medium
    reproduces: false
    source:
      - kind: ac
        id: AC4
    preconditions:
      - Cart total is calculated. An invalid discount code is provided.
    data:
      user: user:standard
    steps:
      - id: S1
        action: POST /cart/discount
        expect:
          description: Attempt to apply a discount code that does not exist.
          status: 404
          fields:
            error_code: DISCOUNT_NOT_FOUND
            total: The total remains unchanged from the state before this request.
    evidence:
      - response
open_questions: []
out_of_scope: []
existing_coverage: []
selection: []
"
